# Forms & i18n

## Validation

- Zod v4 schemas as **factory functions**: `createLoginSchema(t: TFunction)`
- Export inferred types: `type LoginSchema = z.infer<ReturnType<typeof createLoginSchema>>`
- Wire with `zodResolver(schema)` in `useForm`
- Rebuild schema when language changes: `useMemo(() => createXSchema(t), [t])`
- Shared validation keys live under `validation.*` in translation files

## Form pattern

```tsx
const schema = useMemo(() => createLoginSchema(t), [t])
const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors, isSubmitting } } = useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema),
})
```

- Complex inputs (phone) use `Controller` + custom components
- Cross-field rules use `.refine()` (e.g. password confirmation)
- Display errors via `<Field data-invalid={!!errors.field}>` + `<FieldError />`

## i18n

- Init in `src/i18n/index.ts`; imported as side-effect in `main.tsx`
- Languages: `en` (fallback), `sr` — keep both files in sync
- Usage: `const { t } = useTranslation()` → `t('auth.login.title')`
- Language switch: `i18n.changeLanguage()` in settings; persist via API when available
- `Accept-Language` is sent on every API request via `lib/axios.ts`

## Translation key structure

```
common.*       — shared labels (email, password, actions)
validation.*   — form validation messages
auth.*         — login, register, forgot/reset password
layout.*       — sidebar, navigation
<feature>.*    — per-domain copy (screens, media, playlists, etc.)
```
